<% content_for :title, "How it works" %>

<div class="page page--narrow prose">
  <h1>Know what happens next? Bet on it.</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Tolchu turns short clips into tiny prediction markets. Watch the setup, call the next moment,
    and see the result play out a few seconds later.
  </p>

  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <h2>Watch the clip</h2>
      <p>Every clip freezes right before the action: the free throw, the kickflip, the penalty kick. Everything you need to know is on screen.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Make your call</h2>
      <p>Pick one of 2–4 outcomes and stake up to <%= credits(Bet::MAX_STAKE) %>. Betting locks before the play starts, so nobody gets to bet on something they've already seen.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Win from the pool</h2>
      <p>Everyone's stakes go into one shared pool. When the result is in, the correct predictions split it in proportion to what they staked.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>The house never bets against you</h2>
  <p>
    Sportsbooks set odds and profit when you lose. Tolchu is <strong>parimutuel</strong>: the house takes a flat
    <strong>5% fee</strong> from the pool and has no stake in the outcome. The odds come from the crowd.
    The more people back an outcome, the smaller its payout.
  </p>

  <h2>A worked example</h2>
  <div class="example-card">
    <p>“Will the free throw go in?”</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Alice stakes <strong>100</strong> on <em>Swish</em></li>
      <li>Bob stakes <strong>50</strong> on <em>Swish</em></li>
      <li>Carol stakes <strong>50</strong> on <em>Brick</em></li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The pool is <strong>200</strong>. The 5% fee is <strong>10</strong>, leaving <strong>190</strong>.
      It's a swish, so Alice gets <strong>126</strong> (she put in ⅔ of the winning money)
      and Bob gets <strong>63</strong>. Payouts are rounded down. The leftover credit goes to the house.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Fair-play rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Stake cap:</strong> at most <%= credits(Bet::MAX_STAKE) %> per market, so no one can swing a pool on their own.</li>
    <li><strong>Hard lock:</strong> bets are refused the instant a market locks, even from a page that was already open.</li>
    <li><strong>No contest, no fee:</strong> if nobody picked the winner, or nobody bet against it, every stake is refunded in full.</li>
    <li><strong>Winners never lose money:</strong> the fee is capped at what the losing side staked.</li>
    <li><strong>Creators can't bet</strong> on their own markets.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>For creators</h2>
  <p>
    Post a clip from the <%= link_to "studio", studio_markets_path %> and you earn up to <strong>half of the fee</strong> on your market.
    The more evenly the crowd splits, the bigger your cut, so the best clips are the ones that are hard to call.
  </p>

  <p class="muted">Tolchu uses free play-money credits. Every new account starts with <%= credits(User::STARTING_CREDITS) %>.</p>
</div>
